.TH SPS.CONF 5 "2026-08-30" "SPS 1.0" "SPS File Formats"
.SH NAME
sps.conf, repos.conf \- SPS configuration and repository declarations
.SH DESCRIPTION
SPS configuration is line-oriented text, not shell code. Blank lines and lines
beginning with
.B #
are ignored. Each setting is a key followed by whitespace and its value.
.SH GENERAL SETTINGS
.TP
.BI root " path"
Target filesystem root; default
.BR / .
.TP
.BI db " path"
Installed package database; default
.BR /var/lib/sps .
.TP
.BI cache " path"
Source, repository-index, and built-package cache; default
.BR /var/cache/sps .
.TP
.BI build " path"
Temporary build/staging root; default
.BR /var/tmp/sps .
.TP
.BI makejobs " count"
Positive per-package build parallelism exported to recipes as
.BR MAKEJOBS .
.TP
.BI compression " type"
Package compression:
.BR auto ,
.BR none ,
.BR gzip ,
.BR xz ,
or
.BR zstd .
.B zst
is accepted as an alias for zstd.
.TP
.BI arch " name"
Target/build architecture. The default is the local result of
.BR "uname -m" .
Packages marked
.B any
or
.B noarch
are architecture-independent.
.TP
.BI preserve " prefixes"
Comma-separated package-relative path prefixes whose locally modified regular
files are not silently replaced/deleted. Default:
.BR etc .
Use
.B none
to disable the policy.
.SH REPOSITORIES
A declaration has the form:
.PP
.nf
repo NAME PATH [PRIORITY]
.fi
.PP
PATH is a local directory tree. Larger numeric priorities win; configuration
order breaks equal priorities. Repository transport is outside SPS.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR SPS_ROOT ,
.BR SPS_DB ,
.BR SPS_CACHE ,
.BR SPS_BUILD ,
.BR SPS_MAKEJOBS ,
.BR SPS_COMPRESSION ,
.BR SPS_ARCH ,
and
.B SPS_PRESERVE
override corresponding file settings. Set
.B SPS_CONFIG
or
.B SPS_REPOS_CONFIG
to select alternate files.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
root /
db /var/lib/sps
cache /var/cache/sps
build /var/tmp/sps
makejobs 8
compression zstd
preserve etc

repo core  /usr/src/core  100
repo local /usr/src/local 200
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR src (1),
.BR sget (1),
.BR mkpkg (1)
